{"name":"North Rim","hex":"#d8a892","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"north","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The direction towards the pole to the left-hand side of someone facing east, specifically 0°, or (on another celestial object) the direction towards the pole lying on the northern side of the invariable plane.","The up or positive direction."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the north; northern.","Toward the north; northward."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/north"},{"term":"rim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nyaturu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edge around something, especially when circular.","A wheelrim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grand Canyon National Park","blocks":[{"text":"Grand Canyon National Park is a national park of the United States located in northwestern Arizona, the 15th site to have been named as a national park. The park's central feature is the Grand Canyon, a gorge of the Colorado River, which is often considered one of the Wonders of the World. The park, which covers 1,217,262 acres of unincorporated area in Coconino and Mohave counties, received more than 4.9 million recreational visitors in 2024. The Grand Canyon was designated a World Heritage Site by UNESCO in 1979. The park celebrated its 100th anniversary on February 26, 2019."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Dawn_on_the_S_rim_of_the_Grand_Canyon_%288645178272%29.jpg/330px-Dawn_on_the_S_rim_of_the_Grand_Canyon_%288645178272%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Canyon_National_Park","wikidata":"Q220289"},{"title":"North","blocks":[{"text":"North is one of the four compass points or cardinal directions. It is the opposite of south and is perpendicular to east and west. North is a noun, adjective, or adverb indicating direction or geography."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Compass_Rose_English_North.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_North.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North","wikidata":"Q659"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1938 poster of the park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand_Canyon_poster_1938.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/ATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.jpg/500px-ATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/ATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.jpg/500px-ATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grand Canyon quarter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AATBQ_2010_AZ_GrandCanyon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg/1280px-Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Grand_Canyon_Powell_Point_Evening_Light_02_2013.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_Powell_